From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KB2UKA <kb2uka80@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:36:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 16/41] wifi: brcmfmac: Accept bss_info versions up to 116

brcmf_inform_bss() drops a whole scan result when its bss_info version
is above BRCMF_BSS_INFO_MAX_VERSION. The BCM4388 C2 firmware shipped for
the 13-inch MacBook Air (M4, J713) reports version 116, so every scan
came back empty:

  brcmfmac: BSS info version 116 unsupported

Raise the limit to 116. The driver reads the fixed fields at the start
of struct brcmf_bss_info_le and finds the IEs through ie_offset; with
this change a scan lists the nearby networks and association works.

Based on work from Omarchy-M4-Native
(https://github.com/Kb2uka/Omarchy-M4-Native), released under GPL-2.0.

Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/fwil_types.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/fwil_types.h b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/fwil_types.h
index 7b8f809cd..b37f59ca7 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/fwil_types.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/fwil_types.h
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
 #define BRCMF_ARP_OL_PEER_AUTO_REPLY	0x00000008
 
 #define	BRCMF_BSS_INFO_MIN_VERSION	109 /* min ver of brcmf_bss_info_le struct */
-#define	BRCMF_BSS_INFO_MAX_VERSION	112 /* max ver of brcmf_bss_info_le struct */
+#define	BRCMF_BSS_INFO_MAX_VERSION	116 /* max ver of brcmf_bss_info_le struct */
 #define BRCMF_BSS_RSSI_ON_CHANNEL	0x0004
 
 #define BRCMF_STA_BRCM			0x00000001	/* Running a Broadcom driver */
